I assume that the development team is somewhat responsive to public
opinion,  then?  After all,  I assume your reasons for being on that
team are not simply because you like playing the newest versions first...
If so,  perhaps you folks would be responsive to a vote:  not a a final
arbiter of what happens,  of course,  but more an estimate of just what is
the public sentiment on an issue.

If so,  I call for votes,  e-mailed (NOT POSTED) to me:

Regarding movement onto water,  would you like:

A - No confirmation (current implementation)
B - confirmation (as in for peaceful monsters,  default ON)
C - confirmation (ditto,  except default OFF)

Regarding attacking particular monsters (like floating eyes),  would you
like:

E - No confirmation (current implementation)
F - optional confirmations for each monster name (default off,  of course)


All votes must be received on or before Friday,  June 8th,  to be counted.
A verification note will be sent to all voters,  but I will not make
strenuous efforts to deal with problem return addresses.  I will post the
list of voters and their votes sometime after that date.

(I really don't have time to do this,  but hey!  I love getting e-mail...)
